00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:29.410
Wait, the new season of
"Curb Your Enthusiasm"

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:30.590
it comes out this month.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.423
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:31.423 --> 00:01:33.598
- So tell us about it, what's happening?

00:01:33.598 --> 00:01:35.030
- You know, I can't tell you too much,

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.837
because I'm gonna tell you what I do.

00:01:36.837 --> 00:01:39.640
I am truly, although I'm on the show,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.977
I'm a fan of the show and I'm just,

00:01:41.977 --> 00:01:43.870
I'm a big fan of the show
before I got on the show.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.780
So, when I go to work, you know,

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.420
now, I'm gonna tell you
what they call Larry.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.120
They call Larry, the Hog.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.500
Because Larry will do scenes with me,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.130
but he won't let me do scenes
with anybody else, on my own.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.240
You know what I mean?

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.610
They call him, Richard Lewis
calls Larry, "Larry the Hog".

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.650
So, he hogs up J.B.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.260
So, I watched the show like a fan

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.010
and a lot of times, I don't even know

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.140
who the special guests are or anything.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.310
So, when it comes on,

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.876
I sit there like this, I watch the show.

00:02:11.876 --> 00:02:13.240
And I don't want to know everything.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.080
I hate knowing everything.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.080
You know, you know how actors are.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.480
Sometimes actors don't
even watch themselves,

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.590
because they just,

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.135
they feel like they
could've done it better.

00:02:22.135 --> 00:02:22.968
- Yeah.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:23.801
- [Kelly] Yeah, we're hard on ourselves.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:27.060
- We change, we change over a few months.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.640
We become better actors.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.150
You know, we'll see
something a year later,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.664
like, "I did that?
Why's my hand like this?

00:02:33.664 --> 00:02:36.900
Why am I doing this? Oh, I hate myself".

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.733
You know?

00:02:37.733 --> 00:02:39.160
- Why do I look like a sloth when I sing?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.085
Yeah, I don't know.

00:02:40.085 --> 00:02:41.510
- [J.B.] Right, right, we judge ourselves.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.550
So, I tend to watch the
show and a lot of times,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:49.190
because the show's improvised,
I don't remember what I said.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.320
So, sometimes on the way home, you know,

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:52.730
my wife would call me on the way home

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.510
and she'll say, "How was your day?"

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.950
I'll say, "Oh, it was great".

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.227
And she'll always say,
"What did Leon say today?"

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.100
My character, she's like,
"What did Leon say today?"

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.300
Not, "What did J.B. say?",
"What did Leon say today?"

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.621
And I'm like, "Ooh, what
did Leon say today?"

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.910
(audience laughs)

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:10.743
- You have no idea.

00:03:10.743 --> 00:03:13.020
- It's cool that I just
separate the two characters,

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.370
myself and my character I play,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.092
I love telling her what Leon said.

00:03:17.092 --> 00:03:18.181
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:18.181 --> 00:03:21.927
You know? I like that guy.
(audience laughs)

